From 22132d166d93efcee00e014422a87371a96e4f03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:05:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(b4): make login timing uniform; async scrypt
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

verifyLocalUser returned early for an unknown email while running scryptSync
(~25ms) only for a known one (~0.01ms) — a ~2000x timing leak that let
accounts be enumerated. scryptSync also blocked the event loop ~25ms per
attempt.

Switch password hashing/verification to async crypto.scrypt (promisified),
which never blocks the event loop. For an unknown email, verify against a
fixed dummy scrypt hash with identical parameters before returning null, so
an unknown account costs the same as a wrong password (constant-time compare
via timingSafeEqual). Routes await the now-async functions.

Tests: a new timing test asserts unknown vs known-wrong ratio < 3x over 10
iterations; a new non-blocking test proves verification yields to the event
loop (a short timer fires while verification is pending). Existing
login/signup/audit/migrate suites updated to await the async API. tsc 0
errors, npm test passes (only pre-existing environmental desktop-proxy
ECONNRESET flakes fail), build OK.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
